#lang rmn/v2
(map
  ("type" "RecursiveInfomaterialFabricationLaw")
  ("version" 9)
  ("precondition" "The customer supplies exact signed Agent Card URLs for one independent synthesis die, one independent hierarchical-circuit-equivalence assay die, the plate and cover dies, and one provider-law-specific canonical RMN request plus patch-evidence provider per direct mount, with finite frontier and parallelism bounds. Every provider Agent Card carries one placement-neutral sovereign black-box leaf with one valid JWS signature and same-origin RFC 7517 JWKS. A patch provider may be a direct observation die or another recursively composed board occupying the same patch-evidence tensor socket. The board owns only its root and tensor tally membrane profiles.")
  ("operation" "Discover and verify every provider-owned signed Agent Card; hire the recursive observation-circuit synthesis die with exact root, tally, plate, cover, and route-ordered patch-provider interfaces; accept no locally synthesized topology; hire the independent equivalence die for the returned exact family and assembly before material access; then hire the plate provider, verify the direct frontier, require total injective-by-mount routing, transmit each provider's exact canonical RMN request under the parallelism bound, require canonical direct-or-composed patch evidence and root-kind agreement, and hire the cover provider with those exact receipts. Read no material or child interior locally.")
  ("postcondition" "Return the cover provider's canonical patch-evidence RMN receipt and append one typed board receipt binding the synthesis provider and seam, exact recursive circuit and sovereign assembly identities, independent equivalence provider, receipt, and seam, signed provider-card evidence, every patch-provider seam, and every route. The board is itself admissible in any parent patch-provider socket. No local topology, equivalence, cover identity, or alternative material ontology is created.")
  ("refusal" "Refuse synthesis or equivalence without distinct signed typed receipts binding exact inputs, results, attribution, and replay evidence; an unsigned, invalidly signed, off-origin-keyed, absent, repeated, malformed, caller-supplied, non-leaf, non-equivalent, incompletely populated, or substituted circuit interface or assembly; embedded occurrence identity or disclosed provider interior; missing, duplicate, or unknown routes; a route without exactly one provider and one provider-law-specific relational RMN request; non-HTTP Agent Cards; unsafe bounds; provider refusal; noncanonical or non-patch evidence; kind disagreement; unavailable synthesis, equivalence, or witness journal operation; local material access; direct-import fallback; inferred provider substitution; flat unbounded fan-in; or partial fan-in presented as success. Producer identity neither proves nor disproves correctness."))
